    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d753">

                <pb facs="0702" n="690" xml:id="pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Stettinius Mission/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-22T23:00:00+02:00">April 22, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 22—8:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3341. Deles No. 27. From the Under Secretary. During discussions on Saudi Arabia,
                    Sir Maurice Peterson and Murray agreed British and American economic authorities
                    in Cairo should explore possibility of joint Anglo-American goods subsidy
                    program for Saudi Arabia being guided in principle by standard of 50–50
                    participation so far as this compatible with appropriate assignment of loading
                    areas. If Department perceives no objection I suggest Landis be authorized to
                    discuss the question in this sense with Jordan in reference to Cairo’s 995,
                    April 22 [<hi rendition="#italic">21</hi>], 2 p.m. repeating to Department
                    Cairo’s 44 same date to London.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department. Repeated to Jidda and to Cairo for Landis. [Stettinius.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
